tags: bitstream, fpga

A setting of a device: a bitstream that the node loads into the device (for example an
FPGA) before it gives the device to the instance.

The value is the path of the file in the filesystem of the service: the segments
separated by "/", with no "/" at the start. Example: opt/fpga/design.bit.

With no setting, the node loads nothing. The node is bound: it refuses the start if it
cannot load the file.

=== formal
class=setting
default=absent: the node loads nothing
name=bitstream
place=service.container.devices.policies
rule=the node loads the bytes of the file into the device before it gives the device to the instance
value=a relative pathname (definition 3.311 (Relative Pathname) of the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:5dd925be58ed836308859cb1796d9006a7ff6b32eaa1281fd0f28c4604773ed9) of a file in the filesystem of the service: its components are separated by '/' (the byte 47), with no '/' at the start
